# Multi-Platform Input

Defines touch, mouse, keyboard, focus, hover, and shortcut behavior across platforms.

## Mandatory rules

- Must support touch-first interaction on mobile and pointer/keyboard on web and desktop.
- Must keep visible focus states for keyboard navigation.
- Should use hover states where they improve desktop/web clarity.
- Must not make actions available only through hover.
- Must use platform-appropriate keyboard types and input actions.
- Should keep form submission accessible from keyboard where practical.
- Must respect safe areas and keyboard insets on mobile.
- Must localize all labels, hints, and input affordances with concise, clinically appropriate terminology.
- Reusable input components must live in `frontend/lib/shared/`; check the shared catalog before creating feature-local wrappers.
- Must use design tokens exclusively for colors, spacing, and typography ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).

## Implementation standard

- Shared components should handle focus, hover, enabled/disabled, and pressed states consistently.
- Shortcut keys may be added at the shell level but must not conflict with browser/system shortcuts.

## Acceptance checklist

- Forms work with keyboard only.
- Menus, dialogs, and dropdowns dismiss predictably.
- Touch targets are practical on mobile.

